          "say": "Now add every side. Tick each one off as you go.",
          "write": "10+5+6+3+4+8 = 36 m"
        },
        {
          "say": "Shortcut. It matches the full rectangle. 2 times 18 is 36.",
          "write": "2 × (10 + 8) = 36 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fencing with a gate",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A farmer fences a 15 by 9 metre paddock, with a 2 metre gate.",
          "write": "15 m by 9 m, 2 m gate",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y7/maths/perimeter-ex4.svg",
          "alt": "A paddock 15 m by 9 m with a 2 m gate gap"
        },
        {
          "say": "First the full perimeter. 15 plus 9 is 24. Double it is 48.",
          "write": "2 × (15 + 9) = 48 m"
        },
        {
          "say": "No fence goes across the gate. Take off 2 metres.",
          "write": "48 − 2 = 46 m",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Paddock with the gate gap removed",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 440,
                "h": 220,
                "fill": "white"
              },
              {
                "kind": "line",
                "x": 260,
                "y": 260,
                "x2": 320,
                "y2": 260,
                "color": "red",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 290,
                "text": "2 m gate",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "red",
                "anchor": "middle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So the farmer needs 46 metres of fencing.",
          "write": "46 m of fence"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Don't just add the two marked sides. A rectangle has four sides.",
          "write": "✗ 9 + 4 = 13"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't mix units. Change 50 centimetres to 0.5 metres first.",
          "write": "2 m + 50 cm = 2.5 m"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't multiply length by width. That's area, the space inside.",
          "write": "perimeter ≠ area"
        },
        {
          "say": "Perimeter is a length. Write centimetres, not square centimetres.",
          "write": "cm, not cm²"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Peri means around. Perimeter is the around measure.",
          "write": "peri = around"
        },
        {
          "say": "Perimeter is the fence. Area is the grass inside.",
          "write": "fence vs grass"
        },
        {
          "say": "Rectangle: two times, length plus width. Square: four times the side.",
          "write": "2(l + w)   4s"
        },
        {
          "say": "Trace around with your finger and tick off each side.",
          "write": "tick and trace ✓"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
